<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Épila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">21 July <a href="/years/1348">1348</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Épila was fought on 21 July 1348 near Épila in Aragon. King Peter IV defeated the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-aragon">Union of Aragon</a>, the league of nobles and towns that had forced him to confirm its privileges. After the victory Peter annulled the Privileges of the Union, and the league was ended for good.</p></div>
